2026-09-23T17:10:31.7276149Z     The ``pytest`` framework makes it easy to write small tests, yet
2026-09-23T17:10:31.7276621Z     scales to support complex functional testing for applications and libraries.
2026-09-23T17:10:31.7277014Z     
2026-09-23T17:10:31.7277228Z     An example of a simple test:
2026-09-23T17:10:31.7277477Z     
2026-09-23T17:10:31.7277685Z     .. code-block:: python
2026-09-23T17:10:31.7277919Z     
2026-09-23T17:10:31.7278131Z         # content of test_sample.py
2026-09-23T17:10:31.7278406Z         def inc(x):
2026-09-23T17:10:31.7278631Z             return x + 1
2026-09-23T17:10:31.7278862Z     
2026-09-23T17:10:31.7279045Z     
2026-09-23T17:10:31.7279239Z         def test_answer():
2026-09-23T17:10:31.7279488Z             assert inc(3) == 5
2026-09-23T17:10:31.7279729Z     
2026-09-23T17:10:31.7279909Z     
2026-09-23T17:10:31.7280113Z     To execute it::
2026-09-23T17:10:31.7280321Z     
2026-09-23T17:10:31.7280511Z         $ pytest
2026-09-23T17:10:31.7280813Z         ============================= test session starts =============================
2026-09-23T17:10:31.7281170Z         collected 1 items
2026-09-23T17:10:31.7281403Z     
